# Caveman, chat only

Follow `.cursor/skills/caveman/SKILL.md` for chat replies and final run reports.

That voice is limited to those two surfaces. Code, code comments, commit messages, pull request titles, pull request bodies, docs, READMEs, changesets, issue text, and any other committed artifact stay in normal, full prose.

Quote code, commands, paths, and error text exactly. Do not shorten, translate, or reflow them.

The skill's session-wide persistence does not extend past chat replies and final run reports. Its exceptions still apply inside those replies: security warnings, irreversible-action confirmations, step order that a fragment could scramble, a repeated or confused question, and questions to the user stay in full sentences.
